I've lived off of MRE's for over a week on end.  Many other people
have lived on them for longer.  I can tell you that one, all of the
information is very true; two, don't EVER take the frankfurters;
three, schezuan chicken for breakfast is absolutely fine.  What isn't
mentioned in that is that all of the MRE's also include a packet that
contains among other things, coffee, matches, moist towellets (we
usually collect these and give them to any women in our group), toilet
paper (never enough) tabasco, salt, pepper, some sort of bread
product, usually with peanut butter or a fruit-flavored jelly, a fruit
drink (reminiscent of kool-aid), and a candy product like skittles or
M&Ms.  All of this fits snuggly in a pouch small enough to be packed
in the thigh pockets of the Army's Battle Dress Uniform (BDU) which, I
believe should act as a cloak of displacement in dark areas (it's
camoflagued-patterned) and modify your AC -2, in addition to
incorporating some limited capacity for carrying items.  After all
you've got all those pockets.
All in all, the MRE is a wonderful invention, and is currently being
improved yet again, to provide better taste, better nutrition, better
mechanics, and hopefully, for the love of God, get rid of those
blasted frankfurters!

